2026-09-27T03:28:11.0527425Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0527931Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0528363Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0529780Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0531124Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0531262Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0531541Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0531967Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0532351Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0532486Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0532780Z ================
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0532963Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0533203Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0533737Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0534072Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0534229Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0534632Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0534906Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0535112Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0535684Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0536201Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0537173Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0537997Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0538198Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0538916Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0539989Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0540531Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0541024Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0541704Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0541958Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0542248Z ========
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0542407Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0545252Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0547515Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0547898Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0548676Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0549668Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0550672Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0551627Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0552364Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0638031Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0638766Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0639219Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0639649Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0641421Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0643378Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0644346Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0645666Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:28:11.0645973Z 
